        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### ROI model\n\n- **Productivity**: compare **Merged PRs** and **time-to-merge** of *engaged vs passive* developers and *before/after rollout* (baseline stored in Elasticsearch).\n- **External benchmarks**: ~**+40.5%** merged PRs in heavy-use weeks (GitHub×arXiv 2026); **+78%** PRs moving from *code-first → agent-first* (impact dashboard).\n- **Formula**: `ROI = (time saved × cost/hour) − investment` per month. Investment = engineering cost (**Avg monthly investment** panel) plus the **Budget**, **Products** and **LLMs** views below.\n- **Bottom line good scenario**: adoption up, time-to-merge down, merged PRs up, spend at/under budget. **Bad scenario**: licenses paid, acceptance stalled, no throughput lift — while Products and LLM spend overrun the budget: cost without payoff.\n- **Caution**: metrics are directional. Check the **Rework** panel before crediting any gain.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "11.1.0",
      "title": "How to read ROI (modeling)",
      "type": "text"
    },
